        "text": "{\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"reasons\":[\"The gap is real: 14.2(a)(iii), (iv) and (vi) impose one-way obligations on Ono (deliver Data/Ono Know-How, hand over customer data, return or destroy Array's Confidential Information and Product Materials), and no cited or referenced provision obliges Array to return, export, delete or certify deletion of Ono's Data or Confidential Information. With no data-return mechanic on the counterparty at all, the fallback (export within 30 days) is not met, so a 'missing' classification with an insert is the correct call rather than over-flagging an acceptable fallback.\",\"The redline is actionable and minimal in form: a single new reciprocal subsection placed at the end of Section 14.2 tracking the model language (up to 6 months' assistance at Array's then-current rates, return within 30 days in machine-readable format, then deletion with written certification), leaving all existing text untouched.\",\"The drafting respects the negotiated bargain: it expressly carves out Data and Ono Know-How Array is licensed or entitled to retain under 14.2(a)(iii) and (v), makes assistance elective ('at Ono's request') and paid, and mirrors the existing one-archival-copy concession in 14.2(a)(vi), so it does not reopen the licence grant or create an unbalanced obligation.\",\"Deterministic checks pass (operation applies; data-return/transition language present) and the comment is concise, first-person plural, cites the playbook position and offers the 90-day fallback.\",\"Minor points that do not defeat the finding: the comment's statement that nothing obliges Array 'to help us transition' slightly overstates matters given the mutual cooperation covenant in 14.2(a)(iv) (the rationale correctly acknowledges it and explains why it is inadequate), and the rule's detection guidance is framed for services/hosting agreements, so applying it to a pharma licence is a stretch — but the substantive reciprocity gap on return of our Data and Confidential Information is genuine.\",\"Residual drafting risk to confirm on execution: the insertion assumes Section 14.2 does not already contain a subsection (b) (the anchor paragraph p0667 was not included in the supplied original paragraphs), so the sub-numbering should be verified against the full Section 14.2.\"]}"
      }
